WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:06.060
A tragic passing, a secret wedding, and&nbsp;
one last heartbreaking phone call — here's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.560
what went down in the final conversation&nbsp;
between Ryan Coogler and Chadwick Boseman.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.840
The release of Black Panther: Wakanda Forever is&nbsp;
sure to be one of the most emotional outings in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:22.200
the MCU so far. The original film was a massive&nbsp;
success for the franchise, earning over $1.3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:28.020
billion worldwide, and almost guaranteeing a&nbsp;
sequel in the process. Confirmation of a second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:33.540
movie came in October 2018, with The Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter noting that Ryan Coogler had signed a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:39.420
deal to direct and write the second film. THR also&nbsp;
noted around that time that Chadwick Boseman was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:45.780
negotiating a deal for $10 million for the sequel&nbsp;
and $20 million for a third Black Panther film.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.140
So much has changed in the years&nbsp;
since the sequel was given the go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.880
with the MCU fandom still reeling from&nbsp;
the loss of Boseman, who died of colon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.740
cancer in 2020. These emotions are sure&nbsp;
to come flooding back in with the release&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:03.060
of Wakanda Forever, which will deal with&nbsp;
the aftermath of King T'Challa's death.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.680
Ryan Coogler had a lot on his plate with&nbsp;
handling the sequel. The director recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:12.720
appeared on an episode of Wakanda Forever: The&nbsp;
Official Black Panther Podcast to discuss the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.440
upcoming film at length. Boseman is at&nbsp;
the heart of the discussion, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.140
and Coogler even recounts their last phone call.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.240
When author and host Ta-Nehisi Coates asks&nbsp;
Coogler when he finished writing the script&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.040
for Wakanda Forever, Coogler admits he was&nbsp;
done with it before Chadwick Boseman passed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.560
which obviously prompted a major rewrite. Coates&nbsp;
subsequently asks what Boseman said when Coogler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.480
called him to see if he wanted to read the&nbsp;
script. After a long silence, Coogler says:

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:43.740
"He was tired, bro. I could tell he was tired."

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.400
Coogler says that he had been trying&nbsp;
to get a hold of Boseman for a few days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.220
before they finally connected&nbsp;
for what would be their last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.120
phone call. Referring to Boseman's&nbsp;
wife, Simone Ledward, Coogler said:

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.420
"He kicked Simone out cause he told her he didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.060
want her to hear nothing that could&nbsp;
get him in trouble with his NDA."

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.260
Coogler adds:

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.460
"And she didn't wanna leave him.&nbsp;
So I could tell something was up."

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.820
Coogler says that Boseman and Ledward&nbsp;
were planning their wedding in South&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:14.880
Carolina — according to Us Weekly, the duo wed&nbsp;
just a few months before Boseman died. Boseman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.740
then asked Coogler about his child, as he had&nbsp;
missed the baby shower that had just been held.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:25.320
After talking about weddings and children, Ryan&nbsp;
Coogler and Chadwick Boseman's conversation moved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:30.180
on to the Black Panther sequel. According to&nbsp;
Coogler, Boseman said he didn't want to read the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:34.740
finished script because he didn't want to get in&nbsp;
the way of any notes the studio might have, so he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:39.060
said he would read it after they did. The director&nbsp;
later found out that Boseman couldn't read the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:44.460
script because he was just too tired. Coates then&nbsp;
asked how soon after the phone call Boseman died.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:48.600
"A couple of weeks. Yeah, man, a couple of weeks."

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.240
Coogler's manager and agent called and told him,&nbsp;
but he didn't believe it at first, so he called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:59.220
Denzel Washington to check if it was true. He&nbsp;
then texted Boseman, hoping it was a rumor;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:04.560
shortly after, the official press release&nbsp;
went live, and a nightmare became reality.

